      <item>
        <title>Stack plot</title>
        
          <description>&lt;p&gt;A stack plot shows a value/statistic for all 3D annotations in a single &lt;a href=&quot;stack&quot;&gt;stack&lt;/a&gt;. Each point is a value/statistic for one 3D annotation in the stack.&lt;/p&gt;

</description>
        
        <pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2015 15:46:33 -0700</pubDate>
        <link>
        https://mapmanager.github.io/stack-plot</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mapmanager.github.io/stack-plot</guid>
      </item>
      
    
      
      <item>
        <title>Stack Annotations</title>
        
          <description>&lt;p&gt;3D Annotations are the core of Map Manager. They are easy to create, edit, and in a map to connect them between time-points. Annotations can be &lt;a href=&quot;search-panel&quot;&gt;searched&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;map-plot&quot;&gt;plotted&lt;/a&gt;, and exported.&lt;/p&gt;

</description>
        
        <pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2015 15:46:33 -0700</pubDate>
        <link>
        https://mapmanager.github.io/stack-annotations</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mapmanager.github.io/stack-annotations</guid>
      </item>
      
    
      
      <item>
        <title>Search</title>
        
          <description>&lt;p&gt;The search panel is used to find annotations based on a criterion. Searches can be performed within a single stack or time-series, or across multiple stacks and time-series.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
        
        <pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2015 15:46:33 -0700</pubDate>
        <link>
        https://mapmanager.github.io/search-panel</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mapmanager.github.io/search-panel</guid>
      </item>
      
    
      
      <item>
        <title>Run plot</title>
        
          <description>&lt;p&gt;A run plot is a sequence of &lt;a href=&quot;stack&quot;&gt;stack&lt;/a&gt; windows, one for each session in a timeseries. The purpose of a run plot is to visualize the dynamics between annotations. The image below shows a run plot of spines. Spine # 201 is selected in each of three stack windows corresponding to timepoints.&lt;/p&gt;

</description>
        
        <pubDate>Mon, 20 Apr 2015 15:46:33 -0700</pubDate>
        <link>
        https://mapmanager.github.io/run-plot</link>
        <guid isPermaLink="true">https://mapmanager.github.io/run-plot</guid>
      </item>
      
    
      
